<title>USA: Fort Worth, Texas, bonds yield 5.30 pct in 2007.</title>
<headline>Fort Worth, Texas, bonds yield 5.30 pct in 2007.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co said Thursday it tentatively priced $85.3 million Fort Worth, Texas, refunding bonds at a top yield of 5.30 percent in 2007.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>CITY OF FORT WORTH TEXAS</p>
<p>RE: $85,335,000*</p>
<p>(TARRANT AND DENTON COUNTIES)</p>
<p>GENERAL PURPOSE REFUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1996</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD RECEIVED</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aa		    S&amp;P: AA</p>
<p>    DATED: 11/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 09/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 03/01</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>03/01/1998		  965M    4.25  %	  4.30</p>
<p>03/01/1999	     21,755M    5.50  %	  4.45</p>
<p>03/01/2000	     23,270M    5.50  %	  4.625</p>
<p>03/01/2001	     22,315M    6.00  %	  4.75</p>
<p>03/01/2002	     12,955M    6.00  %	  4.85</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>03/01/2003		   25M    4.90  %	  4.95</p>
<p>03/01/2004		   25M    5.00  %	  5.05</p>
<p>03/01/2005		1,350M    5.00  %	  5.10</p>
<p>03/01/2006		1,340M    5.10  %	  5.20</p>
<p>03/01/2007		1,335M    5.20  %	  5.30</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Tuesday, October 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on December 3, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Pryor, McClendon, Counts &amp; Co., Inc.</p>
<p>Apex Securities, Inc.</p>
<p>Grigsby Brandford &amp; Co., Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
